\chapter{Model}
\newcommand{\scoreA}{F1}
We optimize the \scoreA{} of the classifier. The validation \scoreA{} is reported per fold.
Training stops when \scoreA{} plateaus for three rounds.

\chapter{Validation}
\newcommand{\scoreB}[1]{F1\textsubscript{#1}}
The test score \scoreB{test} is computed once. Cross-validation gives \scoreB{cv} with confidence intervals.
Compared with the training \scoreB{train}, the gap indicates mild overfitting, so we track \scoreB{cv} and \scoreB{train} together.

\chapter{Model}
We optimize the \score{train} of the classifier. The validation \score{val} is reported per fold.
Training stops when \score{val} plateaus for three rounds.

\chapter{Validation}
The test score \score{test} is computed once. Cross-validation gives \score{cv} with confidence intervals.
Compared with the training \score{train}, the gap indicates mild overfitting, so we track \score{cv} and \score{train} together.
